<title>AUSTRIA: Steyr flies sky high with new space order. [CORRECTED 12:15 GMT]</title>
<headline>Steyr flies sky high with new space order. [CORRECTED 12:15 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austria's Steyr-Daimler-Puch AG said on Wednesday its automotive technology unit had won a contract to deliver components for the European space programme Ariane worth some 72 million schillings (corrects from $72 million).</p>
<p>The company said it would deliver special fuel lines and mounting components for 14 flights of the Ariane 5 launcher rocket between 1997 and 1999.</p>
<p>Steyr also had tendered to supply components for the 50 Ariane flights scheduled to take place after 1999.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 53112 274</p>
